From: php56-amzn1-security
Subject: Clear request state freed at shutdown (completes the CVE-2026-109618/109619 backport)

Applies after deb.sury.org's 0261-Avoid-state-corruption-via-bailout.patch. Three parts of the
upstream fix (php/php-src@712e60f9, PHP-7.4) that 0261 leaves out:

- shutdown_executor(): the user error/exception handler stacks and EG(in_autoload) are freed but
  keep pointing at the freed memory. Upstream zeroes the stacks ("may be used by zend_error before
  init_executor"); EG(in_autoload) is reset for the same reason, as in vperetti's 5.6 backport
  (github.com/vperetti/php-cve-2026-109618-109619-backports).
- php_request_shutdown_for_hook(): clears PG(http_globals) like 0261 does in php_request_shutdown().
  No bundled SAPI calls it; third-party ones may.
- multipart_buffer_headers(): isspace((unsigned char)...) as upstream.

---
--- a/Zend/zend_execute_API.c
+++ b/Zend/zend_execute_API.c
@@ -332,6 +332,13 @@
 		}
 	} zend_end_try();
 
+	/* may be used by zend_error before init_executor: the destroy calls above
+	 * free these but leave the pointers set */
+	memset(&EG(user_error_handlers_error_reporting), 0, sizeof(EG(user_error_handlers_error_reporting)));
+	memset(&EG(user_error_handlers), 0, sizeof(EG(user_error_handlers)));
+	memset(&EG(user_exception_handlers), 0, sizeof(EG(user_exception_handlers)));
+	EG(in_autoload) = NULL;
+
 	zend_shutdown_fpu(TSRMLS_C);
 
 	EG(active) = 0;
--- a/main/main.c
+++ b/main/main.c
@@ -1784,6 +1784,8 @@
 		for (i = 0; i < NUM_TRACK_VARS; i++) {
 			if (PG(http_globals)[i]) {
 				zval_ptr_dtor(&PG(http_globals)[i]);
+				/* May be accessed before php_request_startup() */
+				PG(http_globals)[i] = NULL;
 			}
 		}
 	} zend_end_try();
--- a/main/rfc1867.c
+++ b/main/rfc1867.c
@@ -455,7 +455,7 @@
 				key = NULL;
 			} else {
 				key = estrdup(line);
-				do { value++; } while(isspace(*value));
+				do { value++; } while(isspace((unsigned char)*value));
 				smart_str_appends(&buf_value, value);
 			}
 		} else if (buf_value.c) { /* If no ':' on the line, add to previous line */
